ggml : copy the experts of a large batch ahead, on a second stream

Phase 6 of docs/moe-offload-plan.md in EuLLM. When a MUL_MAT_ID's experts
are in host memory (--moe-cache, --cpu-moe, --n-cpu-moe) and the GPU
computes it, the scheduler copies them to the card first: it reads the
router's choice back to the host, which waits for the GPU to drain, then
queues the copy on the GPU's own stream, where nothing computes while it
runs. Reading a long prompt alternates the two for every expert tensor of
every layer.

With LLAMA_MOE_PREFETCH=1, a MUL_MAT_ID of at least
LLAMA_MOE_PREFETCH_MIN_TOKENS tokens (512) reads its experts from one of
LLAMA_MOE_PREFETCH_SLOTS slots in VRAM (2 to 4, default 2, each the size of
the largest expert tensor) instead of from the compute buffer. A second
instance of the GPU backend, a stream of its own, fills the slots a whole
tensor at a time while the splits before them compute. Two events per
slot order a copy after the previous reader of its slot, and the reading
split after the copy; the host waits for neither. The slots are placed
before ggml-alloc runs, which leaves them where they are, at the same
addresses every time.

Off unless set. One GPU and one copy of the graph; anything it needs and
does not find (events, a second stream, VRAM for the slots) turns it off
with one line on stderr, and the scheduler copies as before. The host
experts should be pinned (EuLLM's --no-mmap): a copy from pageable memory
overlaps nothing.

EuLLM patch on llama.cpp 6b7b03a (b11370 + PR #29887).

